# sh101 — tap the PRIO switch twice (LAST → LOW → HIGH), then play 01-overlap's notes.
# Proves the panel switch reaches the AUDIO through the real user path, not just the label: with 0/1/2/3
# taps the four priorities render four distinct shas (ddb9d398da39 / 906eb02d5452 / 4022d3274b84 /
# 61d2812ec935 at 200 frames).
#
# ⚠ THE SHELL TRAP THAT MADE THIS CLIP NECESSARY: generating these scripts with
#   `for i in $(seq 1 $n)` silently emits TWO clicks when n=0, because BSD/macOS `seq 1 0` prints "1 0"
# instead of nothing. So the "zero taps" baseline was actually sitting on HIGH, every variant matched, and
# I nearly wrote up "the priority switch does not reach the audio" as a finding. A trace of mono.prio is
# what caught it. Committed as a file so the click frames are fixed and no loop can lie about them again.
click 9 22 90
click 15 22 90
down 40 x
down 60 z
down 80 b
up 100 z
up 120 b
up 140 x
